  "question": {
    "text": "Compound that will give positive Lassaigne&#39;s test for both nitrogen and halogen is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>HCl</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><mi>HCl</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>HCl</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Lassaigne&#39;s test gives presence of chlorine and nitrogen in organic compound by fusion of organic compound in the presence of sodium. The fused products in this case are:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><mi>HCl</mi><munderover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>fusion</mi><mi>Na</mi></munderover><mi>NaCN</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>NaCl</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCN</mi></math> gives +ve test for nitrogen and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math> gives +ve test for halogen.</p>"
  }
}